{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stinky-blushing-gelding","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py::test_gerrit_internal_webhook_does_not_need_unsupported_plugin_header` carries `@pytest.mark.timeout(3)` (`tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:1827`). Run alone on macOS it takes 2.27 s and 2.58 s (2026-11-20 PST, two runs), so it has under 1 s of headroom. In a loaded `make verify` (worktree w05-fieldmouse, 4 h 10 min wall, 21,537 passed) it hit the 3.0 s limit: \"pytest-timeout expired after 3.0s ... (xdist worker gw2); the worker exits now\", then \"worker 'gw2' crashed\". The change under test did not touch `src/rebar/review_bot`. Found while verifying dogtired-blank-fieldmouse.\n\n## Approach\nMeasure where the test's wall time goes (likely app/server startup) and either remove the slow setup from this test or make its bound reflect what it guards. Do not just raise the number without a measured reason.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The test's measured duration and the cause of its cost are recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n- [ ] The test passes 20 consecutive runs under `make verify`-level parallel load (for example `pytest -n 8` over `tests/unit` with the test included), recorded in a comment.","id":"4020-ce89-21ef-431d","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["flaky"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_gerrit_internal_webhook_does_not_need_unsupported_plugin_header times out at its 3 s mark under load"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795199693159420001,"uuid":"b05309e8-f184-43ff-8e74-2ea3cb6583c7"}